    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87-a4">

                <pb facs="0240" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>

                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 23, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>“To General D<hi rendition="#small-caps">ouay,</hi> “<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Commander of the First Division, Saltillo:</hi></p>
                <p>(After a long talk about wine and brandy intended for the general’s table, the
                    letter continues thus:)</p>
                <p>“Affairs are becoming more and more pleasant in Mexico, I have charge of the
                    Belgians and Austrians, the greatest spendthrifts in the world. There is
                    something in the public horizon, and I think it will lead to Maximilian’s
                    departure. If we retire the German power is lost. Such is the reward of four
                    years of war and labor. I have nothing more to say; but if I could have an
                    interview with you I could tell something that would astonish you.</p>
                <p>“I repeat the assurance, dear general, of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#right">“TISSEROT,” <hi rendition="#italic">Intendent for two
                            months and fourteen days.”</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
